# Content-Security-Policy: why every directive is exactly this wide.
#
# Second lock on a door already locked in code (createElement/createTextNode
# everywhere, SVG allow-listed). This file makes the browser enforce it too.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why _headers, not wrangler.jsonc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# _headers is the Netlify/Pages/Workers spelling — deploy-host-agnostic.
# serve.py sends no headers, so violations are invisible locally.
# tests/csp.test.js is the substitute — it holds hashes and hosts in step
# with the code, so a breaking change fails in `npm test`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# script-src 'self' + seven hashes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No 'unsafe-inline'. Hashes present means browsers ignore the keyword anyway.
#
# Eight hashes cover every inline script the app ships:
#   - index.html pre-paint restore (must run before first paint; cannot be a module)
#   - index.html boot-cover rescue (failsafe when main.js never parses)
#   - index.html JSON-LD (hash arguably unnecessary per spec, but implementations vary)
#   - patch.html two JSON-LD blocks (breadcrumb + article; must not carry
#     anything that changes per release — taken out at v0.195)
#   - lab.html inline module
#   - lab-sound.html inline module (cannot be a file: tests/imports.test.js
#     holds the exception list closed)
#   - lab-grime.html inline module, for the same reason
#
# patch.html shares the pre-paint and boot-rescue scripts byte-for-byte from
# index.html (gen-patch-page.mjs copies them), so those need no extra hashes.
# 404.html is a byte copy of index.html (save.bat). tests/csp.test.js
# recomputes all hashes; tests/notfound.test.js checks 404.html.
#
# No 'unsafe-eval' or 'wasm-unsafe-eval': nothing in the app calls eval.
# Both wasm payloads (ffmpeg, pdf.js JPEG 2000) run in exempted workers below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# style-src 'self' + four hashes — no 'unsafe-inline'
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# One hash per inline <style> block: index.html, lab.html, lab-sound.html,
# lab-grime.html.
# Benches carry their look inline so tests/sw.test.js need not list a debug
# sheet in SHELL. Browsers ignore 'unsafe-inline' when any hash is present.
#
# Editing a <style> block by one byte changes its hash and the deploy silently
# refuses the block. tests/csp.test.js recomputes both directions.
#
# CSSOM writes (style.setProperty) are outside CSP — ui/look.ts and the
# pre-paint script both use that path and are unaffected.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# img-src / media-src / font-src — 'self' plus local schemes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# No remote host in any of the three. Nothing that renders resolves a URL out
# of a document it opened — these directives make that a guarantee.
# A shared board arrives over connect-src first, then becomes blob: URLs like
# everything else, so from first paint it is an ordinary local board.
#
#   img-src 'self' blob: data:
#     blob: — board assets from IndexedDB as object URLs
#     data: — library thumbnails (toDataURL) and CSS SVG glyphs
#   media-src 'self' blob:  — audio/video object URLs
#   font-src 'self' blob:   — blob: is load-bearing: FontFace('url("blob:...")')
#                              IS checked against font-src
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# connect-src 'self' blob: https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://www.googleapis.com
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   'self'      — sw.js caching, stickers.svg fetch
#   blob:       — pigments.ts fetches blob URLs for createImageBitmap
#   jsdelivr    — ffmpeg core (optimize/media.ts probe + media-worker.js fetch)
#   googleapis  — share link: upload to / download from Google Drive
#
# accounts.google.com is NOT here — the sign-in popup is a navigation, not a
# fetch, governed by no CSP directive. tests/csp.test.js NOT_FETCHED list.
# No Google SDK: that would put a remote host in script-src.
#
# Pinned to host, not path — CSP path matching is unreliable.
# Dropping jsdelivr degrades gracefully (mediaAvailable() returns false).
# Dropping googleapis breaks the share link outright.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# frame-src — the two embed hosts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# canvas/embed.ts builds src from a fixed template with a validated id.
# youtube-nocookie.com (privacy host) and open.spotify.com only.
# Not youtu.be or play.spotify.com — input hosts differ from frame hosts.
# tests/csp.test.js checks both directions.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# connect-src — the decorate-a-player-card hosts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# canvas/embed-meta.ts fetches a player card's title from the provider's oembed:
# open.spotify.com for a track, www.youtube.com for a video. Spotify's reply also
# names a cover on i.scdn.co, fetched next. The only network this app reaches to
# decorate a card, and only for one that has no title stored yet - see the
# local-first note in canvas/renderers.ts. Fetched, not navigated and not shown
# as a remote <img>: the cover is stored as an asset and drawn from blob:, which
# is why i.scdn.co is here and not in img-src (which stays 'self' blob: data:).
# YouTube's reply is the title alone, so it needs no img host of its own.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The deliberate 'none's and explicit 'self's
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   object-src 'none'      — no plugins, ever
#   form-action 'none'     — no forms, no server
#   frame-ancestors 'none' — no framing (clickjack risk on a canvas app).
#                            To widen: 'self' https://valjdakosta.com, not '*'
#   base-uri 'self'        — NOT 'none': <base href="/"> is load-bearing for
#                            404 routing. 'none' would break all relative URLs
#   default-src 'self'     — backstop for all unlisted directives
#
# worker-src and manifest-src are explicit 'self' (not left to default-src)
# because both fail silently and a greppable directive is worth the characters.
#
# Omitted on purpose: 'unsafe-eval', 'wasm-unsafe-eval', upgrade-insecure-
# requests, require-trusted-types-for, report-to (no server).

